@prefix : <http://example.org/antigone#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:exodus-translations-1155-1182-english a owl:Ontology .
# English translation variants extracted from 1155_to_1182.ttl

:TV_Line_1155_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "Neighbors of Cadmus and of Amphion's house,"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1155 .

:TV_Line_1156_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "there is no human life whose standing state I could"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1156 .

:TV_Line_1157_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "ever either praise or blame."^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1157 .

:TV_Line_1158_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "For fortune raises up, and fortune casts down"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1158 .

:TV_Line_1159_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "both the fortunate man and the unfortunate, always;"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1159 .

:TV_Line_1160_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "and no prophet knows what is fixed for mortals."^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1160 .

:TV_Line_1161_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "For Creon once was enviable, in my eyes,"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1161 .

:TV_Line_1162_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "after saving this Cadmean land from enemies,"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1162 .

:TV_Line_1163_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "and taking complete rule over the country,"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1163 .

:TV_Line_1164_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "he governed it, flourishing with a noble line of children;"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1164 .

:TV_Line_1165_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "and now all of it is gone. For when men betray"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1165 .

:TV_Line_1166_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "their pleasures, I do not consider such a man"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1166 .

:TV_Line_1167_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "to be alive, but I regard him as a living corpse."^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1167 .

:TV_Line_1168_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "Let him be rich at home, if you wish, greatly rich,"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1168 .

:TV_Line_1169_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "and live with the outward shape of a king; but if the joy"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1169 .

:TV_Line_1170_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "of these things is absent, all the rest I would not buy"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1170 .

:TV_Line_1171_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "from any man for the shadow of smoke, compared with pleasure."^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1171 .

:TV_Line_1172_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "What burden of grief for the royal house do you come bearing?"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1172 .

:TV_Line_1173_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "They are dead; and the living are guilty of their death."^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1173 .

:TV_Line_1174_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "And who has killed? Who lies dead? Speak."^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1174 .

:TV_Line_1175_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "Haemon is dead; his own hand has shed his blood."^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1175 .

:TV_Line_1176_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "By his father's hand, or by his own?"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1176 .

:TV_Line_1177_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "By his own hand, angry with his father for the murder."^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1177 .

:TV_Line_1178_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "O prophet, how truly you fulfilled your word."^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1178 .

:TV_Line_1179_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "Since things stand so, the rest must now be considered."^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1179 .

:TV_Line_1180_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "And now I see poor Eurydice nearby,"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1180 .

:TV_Line_1181_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "the wife of Creon, coming from the house,"^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1181 .

:TV_Line_1182_en a :TranslationVariant ;
    :text "either because she has heard of her son, or by chance."^^xsd:string ;
    :relatedTo :Line_1182 .